WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.150
Tom Cruise's absence from the 2023 Oscars
drew a few jokes from host Jimmy Kimmel.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:10.500
But, really, why wasn't he there considering
all those nominations for "Top Gun: Maverick"?

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:13.260
Did something upset him, or were there other
reasons?

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.450
"Top Gun: Maverick" soared into the Oscars
with six nominations, but star Tom Cruise

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:22.886
wasn't in attendance to see how well the film
fared on the biggest night of the year for movies.

00:00:22.886 --> 00:00:27.840
Deadline was the first to confirm that Cruise
would not be attending the 95th Academy Awards

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.360
because his commitments to his craft and career
forced him to miss the prestigious affair.

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:37.260
Specifically, he was filming in Sicily and
the United Kingdom, completing his work on

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:41.510
"Mission: Impossible – Dead Reckoning Part
Two," the follow-up to the first "Dead Reckoning"

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.471
installment set to release in summer 2023.

00:00:44.471 --> 00:00:47.260
There are high hopes attached to "Dead Reckoning
Part One."

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:50.920
Many hope it will have the same effect on
the box office that "Top: Gun Maverick" had

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.285
when it grossed over $1 billion in 2022.

00:00:54.285 --> 00:00:58.450
"Maverick" not only proved to be the biggest
box office draw of the year, but it also earned

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.840
high-flying scores on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:05.373
On the Oscars red carpet, Cruise's "Maverick"
co-star Charles Parnell said that Cruise was

00:01:05.373 --> 00:01:07.289
"And saving the movie industry while people
are frettin'."

00:01:07.289 --> 00:01:12.049
"Maverick" was nominated for Best Picture,
as well as several other honors, namely, Best

00:01:12.049 --> 00:01:18.488
Adapted Screenplay, Best Sound, Best Film
Editing, Best Original Song, and Best Visual Effects.

00:01:18.488 --> 00:01:23.020
Cruise himself was nominated in the Best Picture
category as one of the film's producers.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.120
"Maverick" didn't end up snagging that award,
but it did win for Best Sound.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.229
While Tom Cruise is hard at work delivering
another big screen spectacle, Oscars host

00:01:31.229 --> 00:01:35.101
Jimmy Kimmel couldn't help but point out how
the superstar skipped the ceremony.

00:01:35.101 --> 00:01:38.750
During his opening monologue, Kimmel called
out the "Top Gun: Maverick" actor and "Avatar:

00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:43.170
The Way of Water" director James Cameron for
not showing up to the year's biggest celebration

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:47.868
of cinema, despite being the two most vocal
supporters of the theatrical experience.

00:01:47.868 --> 00:01:48.823
Kimmel quipped,

00:01:48.823 --> 00:01:53.290
"The two guys who insisted we come to the
theater didn't come to the [Dolby Theatre]."

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:57.640
Kimmel then jokingly suggested that Cruise
disguised himself as actor Judd Hirsch wearing

00:01:57.640 --> 00:02:00.539
one of those uncanny masks from "Mission:
Impossible."

00:02:00.539 --> 00:02:04.939
Hirsch, nominated for Best Supporting Actor
for his role in "The Fablemans," laughed along.

00:02:04.939 --> 00:02:09.470
The host wrapped up by pointing out Cruise's
athletic body in "Top Gun: Maverick" and tying

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:12.051
it into the actor's renowned faith in Scientology.

00:02:12.051 --> 00:02:12.929
Kimmel said,

00:02:12.929 --> 00:02:15.781
"Tom Cruise with his shirt off in that beach
football scene?

00:02:15.781 --> 00:02:17.561
L. Ron Hubba Hubba!"

00:02:17.561 --> 00:02:21.680
Cruise may not have been at the Oscars, but
Lady Gaga certainly was, delivering a mighty

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:26.860
and powerful rendition of her Oscar-nominated
track "Hold My Hand" from the "Maverick" soundtrack.

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.920
It was previously reported that Lady Gaga
would be skipping the event due to her commitments

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.938
to the "Joker" sequel "Joker: Folie à Deux."

00:02:33.938 --> 00:02:39.220
Just hours before the 2023 Oscars began, Variety
confirmed that the pop sensation would take

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.110
the stage to sing "Hold My Hand."

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:45.130
Like the film, the song received significant
critical acclaim, with Variety calling it

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.050
an Oscar front-runner early on.

00:02:47.050 --> 00:02:51.700
It was also well received by fans, especially
considering the music video has more than

00:02:51.700 --> 00:02:54.421
155 million views on YouTube.

00:02:54.421 --> 00:02:58.840
As far as honors go, the song has already
received some awards attention with a nomination

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:00.890
from the Grammy Awards for Best Song Written
for Media.

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:05.500
The "Top Gun: Maverick" soundtrack was also
nominated for Best Compilation Soundtrack

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.689
for Visual Media.

00:03:06.689 --> 00:03:11.220
While it didn't win either of those accolades,
nor the Oscar for Best Original Song, Gaga's

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.530
stripped-down performance was an unforgettable
part of the Academy Awards telecast.

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:19.470
So even though Cruise couldn't make it to
the ceremony, "Top Gun: Maverick" was certainly

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.000
well represented at Hollywood's big night.

